  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Consider the triangle with the given information,</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0023_f21ee95d4e29.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 151px;\" /><br />The slope of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, so the equation of altitude from <math><mi>C</mi></math> is <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math><br />The slope of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></math>, so the&nbsp;equation of altitude from <math><mi>A</mi></math> is <math><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Solving these two equations, we get,&nbsp;<br />orthocentre of the triangle is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"
